ened**\n- I placed one purchase order for 3\u00d7 DK-200 docks and 3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors, shipping to HQ. DK-200 was in stock and new, so DK-210 wasn't needed.\n- The request timed out. The retry with the same idempotency key reported an upstream fulfilment error after the first line item, so the order is incomplete.\n- `list_orders` shows **PO0001**: 3\u00d7 DK-200 docks, $567, ship to HQ, status `partially_placed`. The **3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) are not on any order.**\n\n**Options (I need your call)**\n1. **Place a separate PO for the 3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) to HQ.** This gets the equipment moving. It breaks the single-PO request, though, since the docks and monitors would be on two orders.\n2. **Cancel PO0001 (refund the $567) and place one new PO for both items.** This matches the single-PO request. It depends on the upstream system working this time, and a second failure could leave us in the same spot.\n3. **Hold for now** while you check the upstream fulfilment issue.\n\nBoth totals are under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval is needed for either option. Tell me which you want and I'll proceed.", "type": "text"}]}]}